title: Authorizations › New case › Intake › Possible duplicate
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId (Intake, the one alert)
intro: Intake warns when the case looks like a request that already exists: the same patient, payer and level of care with an open request, a saved draft that has not been sent, or an active authorization whose dates overlap. It never refuses. The person opens the other one, or continues with a short reason, which stays on the case and in the request's History. Only records at the sites in view are compared.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Patient, payer and level of care are in\nThe check runs as soon as they are"
decision d1 "Does another record match?\nSame patient (initials and age, or the patient's id), same payer, same level of care"
process pWhat "What counts as a match\nAn open request: Preparing, Received, Under review or Info requested\nA saved draft not yet sent whose dates overlap\nAn active or expiring authorization whose approved dates overlap the dates asked for"
process pLeft "Left out\nThe case itself\nThe authorization a review, renewal or modification follows\nAnything at a site the viewer cannot see"
endx eNone "No alert\nIntake is Complete when nothing else is open"
screen sBan "Amber alert, the only one on Intake\n'This looks like a request that already exists'\n'R-1042, admission request, being prepared. Summit Medicaid HMO, Residential 3.5.'\n'Same patient, payer and level of care, with dates that overlap. Sending both would ask the payer for the same days twice.'"
process pState "Intake shows Blocked\n'A matching request exists'\nThe footer hint says 'A matching request exists. Open it, or continue with a reason.'"
click cOpen "Click 'Open R-1042'"
process pOpen "A request opens on its case page\nA draft opens in New case"
goto gCase "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
click cWhy "Click 'Continue with a reason'"
input iWhy "Type in 'Why is this a different request?'\n'For example: the first request was for the earlier stay'"
decision dText "Is there a reason?"
process pOff "'Continue with this reason' stays switched off"
click cDo "Click 'Continue with this reason'"
click cCancel "Click 'Cancel'"
process pBack "The box closes; the alert stays"
store st "The reason is saved on the case with what it is about\nThe alert becomes one quiet line"
screen sSaid "'Continuing with a reason. R-1042, ... Your reason: ...'\nButton 'Undo'"
click cUndo "Click 'Undo'"
process pUndo "The alert is back and Intake is Blocked again"
process pRev "Review & submit lists 'Possible duplicate' as a note\n'You went on and said why: ...'\nSending is no longer stopped by it"
store stHist "After sending, the request's History says\n'You sent this request knowing a matching one exists'\n'Your reason: ...'"
process pType "Changing the Authorization type clears the reason\nThe check runs again for the new type"
goto gSign "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Review & submit › Sign and send to payer"
goto gMis "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Review & submit › What is missing"

s1 --> d1
d1 -.-> pWhat
d1 -.-> pLeft
d1 -->|No| eNone
d1 -->|Yes| sBan --> pState
sBan --> cOpen --> pOpen --> gCase
sBan --> cWhy --> iWhy --> dText
dText -->|No| pOff --> iWhy
dText -->|Yes| cDo --> st --> sSaid
iWhy --> cCancel --> pBack --> sBan
sSaid --> cUndo --> pUndo --> sBan
st --> pRev --> gMis
st --> stHist --> gSign
sSaid -.-> pType
